From 352361175a372e65a38316a4ef979a2495c28a01 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 00:04:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] fix(allwinner): stop the watchdog for SYSTEM_OFF

Without a PMIC, SYSTEM_OFF only turns the CPUs off and the SoC stays
powered. A watchdog that the OS left running (Linux with
watchdog.stop_on_reboot=0 and a forced power-off) then resets the
system a few seconds later and it boots again.

Stop the watchdog once the PMIC power-down has not taken effect.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
---
 plat/allwinner/common/sunxi_native_pm.c | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/plat/allwinner/common/sunxi_native_pm.c b/plat/allwinner/common/sunxi_native_pm.c
index 1b95bbf..d2892bc 100644
--- a/plat/allwinner/common/sunxi_native_pm.c
+++ b/plat/allwinner/common/sunxi_native_pm.c
@@ -219,6 +219,12 @@ static void sunxi_system_off(void)
 	/* Attempt to power down the board (may not return) */
 	sunxi_power_down();
 
+	/*
+	 * The power stays on (no PMIC), only the CPUs are turned off. Stop the
+	 * watchdog, or one that the OS left running brings the system back up.
+	 */
+	mmio_write_32(SUNXI_WDOG0_MODE_REG, 0);
+
 	/* Turn off all CPUs */
 	sunxi_cpu_power_off_others();
 	sunxi_cpu_power_off_self();
